@dotdance/dsh-skill-scope README · 它解决什么问题：**dsh-skill-scope 就是为这件事做的**：把「模型能调用哪些 Skill 与 MCP」变成一组
看得见、点得动的开关，并按**全局**和**本工作区**两个粒度分别管理。

---

@dotdance/dsh-skill-scope README · The problem it solves：**dsh-skill-scope exists for exactly this**: it turns "which skills and MCP servers the model can call" into a set of
visible, clickable switches, managed separately at **global** and **per-workspace** scope.

---

@dotdance/dsh-skill-scope README · 1. The global panel — switch off everything no project needs：Click **Global Skills** in the left sidebar to open a native main-view page listing everything at the
**global layer**, skills and MCP servers alike. Anything you switch off here **is off by default in every workspace**;
when one project really needs it, that project can switch it back on (see rule 3).

The red circles above mark the two entry points: **Global Skills** in the left sidebar, and **Workspace Skills** at the bottom right of the input box.

@dotdance/dsh-skill-scope README · 1. The global panel — switch off everything no project needs：- The row at the top is a **view filter** (All / Enabled / Disabled) — it only filters the list, it changes no switch.
- The search box **filters both the Skill and the MCP sections**, live as you type.
- The list groups and collapses by source, so even a long inventory stays navigable.
